<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The two things §6 lets a reader do to a task's place in the tree from the list itself: hang it on the row above,
  or lift it out of the one it hangs on.

  Both titles are replaced when the menu is built — `HierarchyMenu` puts the action's name on a press that would work
  and the *reason* on one that would not, which is how «нельзя indent, если нет допустимого родителя» reaches the
  reader as a sentence rather than as a missing row or a dead button. What is written here is the allowed case, so a
  menu that failed to set its titles says something true about a normal row.

  No "move to" here on purpose. §6.3's destination picker is its own block — it has to draw the topic path, name the
  row's children, and compute the depth before the reader confirms — and smuggling a half version of it next to two
  one-press actions would be the worst of both.
-->
<menu xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <item
        android:id="@+id/action_indent_task"
        android:title="@string/row_indent" />

    <item
        android:id="@+id/action_outdent_task"
        android:title="@string/row_outdent" />
</menu>
